{"id":3911,"date":"2021-10-25T13:56:57","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:56:57","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3911"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:26:21","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:26:21","slug":"2-1-flight-events-senior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-1-flight-events-senior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"2.1: Flight Events"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350003\" name=\"6a22135350003\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251166195{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350136\" name=\"6a22135350136\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Senior Blocks<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In the intermediate module, you will be using the &#8220;Senior&#8221; set of blocks. Now that you have mastered Blockly basics, these blocks will begin to introduce more advanced concepts. Click on the &#8220;Senior&#8221; tab to open up the new set of blocks.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12672&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>You might notice that the blocks might look a little different, but they will do the same commands. This is so you can familiarize yourself with a coding format that more closely resembles Python, a popular text-based programming language.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350197\" name=\"6a22135350197\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight Events<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Flight events include takeoffs, landings, and hovering. You will find these blocks inside the &#8220;Flight Commands&#8221; menu. In this lesson, we will focus on the first four blocks in this list.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12674&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221353501fa\" name=\"6a221353501fa\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Take-Off<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Any code that has your CoDrone EDU in the air will start with the <strong>takeoff()<\/strong> block. This will make your drone launch from the ground. Don\u2019t worry about your drone flying straight into the ceiling! CoDrone EDU uses the height sensor to fly about a meter off of the ground. Then, it will hover automatically and wait for the next command.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7915&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Let\u2019s make your CoDrone EDU take off now! Drag the <strong>takeoff()<\/strong> block from the &#8220;Flight Commands&#8221; menu to your workspace.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9663&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350248\" name=\"6a22135350248\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Land<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The <strong>land()<\/strong> block brings your CoDrone EDU to the ground gently. When you\u2019re finished with everything else in your code, attach the <strong>land()<\/strong> block to the bottom of your program.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9654&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350299\" name=\"6a22135350299\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Hover<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>If you want your CoDrone EDU to hover for more time before landing, you can use the <strong>hover()<\/strong> block from the flight commands menu and connect it after takeoff. <em>Don\u2019t forget to type in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone EDU to hover for before landing.<\/em><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10174&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221353502f5\" name=\"6a221353502f5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wait<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Using the hover command is one way to make your program pause for a duration of seconds. You can also use a <strong>sleep()<\/strong> block, found in the gray \u201cTiming\u201d category. This block will pause your program. In other words, it puts your program to sleep. No other commands will be sent until the time delay finishes.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12675&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Replace <strong>hover()<\/strong> with a <strong>sleep()<\/strong> delay of 3 seconds.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10175&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213535036b\" name=\"6a2213535036b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Emergency Stop Motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1723656640891{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Though this command should only be used in emergencies or when safety has become a concern, in this exercise, try to catch the drone when using the <strong>emergency_stop()<\/strong> block or clicking &#8220;Stop&#8221;. In all other circumstances, you should use the land command to bring your drone safely to the ground.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>There might be times when your CoDrone EDU is about to crash into something, and you need to have it land before it does serious damage. If you want your CoDrone EDU to land before crashing, you can always use the &#8220;Stop&#8221; button in your workspace.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12842&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>You can also use the <strong>emergency_stop()<\/strong> command, located under \u201cFlight Commands\u201d. However, we always recommend using <strong>land()<\/strong>\u00a0whenever possible if you want to protect your drone from damage.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221353503d0\" name=\"6a221353503d0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: CoDrone EDU Pushups\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Try to make your CoDrone EDU take off and land 3 times in a row with one code! Currently, your CoDrone EDU can do one push-up with the code you have.<\/div>\n<div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Rules<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>1. The CoDrone EDU must completely leave the ground on takeoff.<\/div>\n<div>2. The CoDrone EDU must be completely back on the ground on landing.<\/div>\n<div>3. You must include a hover command between takeoff and landing.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22135350420\" name=\"6a22135350420\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In this lesson, you had your first look at programming CoDrone EDU to take off, hover, and land using senior level blocks. You might have noticed that the blocks look different from the junior level blocks. Don\u2019t worry, they were designed to help you get used to how functions look in text-based programming languages like Python and JavaScript!<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251166195{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-1-flight-events-senior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,4328,14401,2112,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-3911","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-flight-events","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-intermediate","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3911","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":36,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3911\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13623,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3911\/revisions\/13623"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4739"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3911"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3911"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3911"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}